.SS " \fBMessage\fP babel\&.messages\&.catalog\&.Catalog\&.add ( self, \fB_MessageID\fP id, \fB_MessageID\fP | None  string = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[tuple[str, int]]  locations = \fC()\fP, Iterable[str]  flags = \fC()\fP, Iterable[str]  auto_comments = \fC()\fP, Iterable[str]  user_comments = \fC()\fP, \fB_MessageID\fP  previous_id = \fC()\fP, int | None  lineno = \fCNone\fP, str | None  context = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Add or update the message with the specified ID\&.

>>> catalog = Catalog()
>>> catalog\&.add(u'foo')
<Message \&.\&.\&.>
>>> catalog[u'foo']
<Message u'foo' (flags: [])>

This method simply constructs a `Message` object with the given
arguments and invokes `__setitem__` with that object\&.

:param id: the message ID, or a ``(singular, plural)`` tuple for
           pluralizable messages
:param string: the translated message string, or a
               ``(singular, plural)`` tuple for pluralizable messages
:param locations: a sequence of ``(filename, lineno)`` tuples
:param flags: a set or sequence of flags
:param auto_comments: a sequence of automatic comments
:param user_comments: a sequence of user comments
:param previous_id: the previous message ID, or a ``(singular, plural)``
                    tuple for pluralizable messages
:param lineno: the line number on which the msgid line was found in the
               PO file, if any
:param context: the message context

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterable[tuple[\fBMessage\fP, list[\fBTranslationError\fP]]] babel\&.messages\&.catalog\&.Catalog\&.check ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Run various validation checks on the translations in the catalog\&.

For every message which fails validation, this method yield a
``(message, errors)`` tuple, where ``message`` is the `Message` object
and ``errors`` is a sequence of `TranslationError` objects\&.

:rtype: ``generator`` of ``(message, errors)``

.fi
